# Mobile — installed UI first

`VStack` and `HStack` stay the layout. They are already the wrappers for this app.

Before adding a control, use the installed component that is the normal choice for that job.

- If `@expo/ui` has it, use it. That means SwiftUI on iOS (menus, sheets, pickers, sliders, buttons).
- If a dedicated package in this app is the normal tool, use that package. Images use `expo-image`. Long lists use `@shopify/flash-list`.
- A custom control is only for an interaction none of those can do. The mini-player drag, from the collapsed bar into the full player, is that case. A menu, sheet, or image next to it is not.

## Examples

```tsx
// Wrong: a hand-built modal for track actions
<Modal>{/* Play, Play next, Add to queue */}</Modal>

// Right: Expo UI. SwiftUI Menu on iOS.
import { Host, Menu, Button } from "@expo/ui/swift-ui";
```

```tsx
// Wrong: React Native Image
import { Image } from "react-native";

// Right
import { Image } from "expo-image";
```
